    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(g(x))=x-5$, with domain $[2,\\infty)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=(\\sqrt{x-2})^2-3\\\\f(g(x))&=x-5\\end{align*}$$\nSince the domain of $g(x)$ is restricted to $x\\geq2$, the domain of $f(g(x))$ is also restricted to $x\\geq2$.",
